# coordinate.config — config for coordinate.sh, the deterministic cross-stage
# coordinator. Copy to coordinate.config and edit. Sourced by bash, so:
# VAR=value, no spaces around '='.
#
# coordinate.sh validates EVERY value before doing anything else (design §11)
# and never `eval`s a configured command — command prefixes are data, appended
# to a safely-constructed argv. Run `coordinate.sh doctor --config <path>` to
# diagnose this file in place (read-only; touches network only for one fetch).
#
# SCOPE: one coordinator watches one target repository. The watcher and the
# three role clones (CC / Pi / Codex) MUST all resolve to the SAME normalized
# remote identity and trunk branch — coordinate.sh normalizes https/ssh/scp-like
# forms of the same remote to one canonical key (design §5, §11).

# A local clone of the target repo used ONLY for observation. The coordinator
# fetches origin/<BRANCH> here and reads via `git show` — it never checks out
# or writes target state. Must be an independent clone, not one of the role
# clones below.
OBSERVER_WORKDIR=/absolute/path/to/observer-clone

# Trunk branch (where .pipeline metadata + journal live). Often main/master.
# Every clone below must agree on this branch.
BRANCH=main

# Independent local clones backing the three long-lived role panes. Each has a
# stable absolute path and a unique Herdr pane whose cwd is that clone (or a
# descendant of it). All four workdirs (observer + these three) must share one
# normalized remote identity.
CC_WORKDIR=/absolute/path/to/cc-clone
PI_WORKDIR=/absolute/path/to/pi-clone
CODEX_WORKDIR=/absolute/path/to/codex-clone

# Optional runtime-issued pane pins. cwd discovery is used when a pin is unset;
# when set, the pin overrides discovery but MUST still resolve to that role's
# clone and MUST NOT be the pane running coordinate.sh itself. Pane ids are
# runtime-issued and die with the pane — re-pin from `herdr pane list`.
# CC_PANE_ID=wA:p1
# PI_PANE_ID=wB:p1
# CODEX_PANE_ID=wC:p1

# Stage command prefixes for each role. Non-empty single-line strings; the
# coordinator appends the escaped dispatch envelope (repo/branch/feature/seq/
# commit) as data — these are never interpreted by a shell.
CC_ARCH_CMD=/pipeline-arch
CC_TASK_CMD=/pipeline-task
CC_HUNT_CMD=/pipeline-hunt
PI_IMPL_CMD=/skill:pipeline-impl
CODEX_REVIEW_CMD='$pipeline-review'

# Polling / readiness / stage budgets. Positive base-10 integers.
# POLL_SECS: no-change Git polling interval (no change is not an error).
# PANE_READY_TIMEOUT_MS: bound for waiting to deliver before the stage begins (<= 600000).
# STAGE_TIMEOUT_SECS: bound on a delivered stage producing neither a newer journal
#                     entry nor a valid human-merge wait (<= 86400).
POLL_SECS=30
PANE_READY_TIMEOUT_MS=60000
STAGE_TIMEOUT_SECS=2700

# Optional halt hook: invoked as an argv vector (no shell expansion) with the
# SOLE argument being the absolute halt.json path, under a bounded timeout. Must
# be an absolute, executable, REGULAR file (never a symlink) when set. It
# receives no prompts/tokens and cannot authorize resume.
# ON_HALT_EXEC=/absolute/path/to/notifier

# Optional state root (default: ${XDG_STATE_HOME:-$HOME/.local/state}/pipeline-driver).
# MUST be outside every configured clone. Created 0700; files 0600. Writes reject
# symlink destinations and use exclusive random same-directory temp files.
# STATE_DIR=/absolute/path/to/pipeline-driver-state

# Optional per-watcher overrides of the machine bindings in drive.defaults
# (see drive.defaults.example): CC_AGENT / CC_MODEL_EXPECT / IMPL_AGENT /
# IMPL_MODEL_EXPECT / REVIEW_AGENT / REVIEW_MODEL_EXPECT. config wins.
# *_MODEL_EXPECT is a literal case-insensitive ASCII substring (printable ASCII
# only — control bytes and bytes ≥0x80 are rejected); *_AGENT is [A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]*.
